-- 0077_conga_why_and_tradeoff.sql
-- Mark 2026-11-25: a ship card cannot show a 3.6 and then slam the ship in one quoted sentence.
-- The card shows two parts instead: "Why this ship" (the upside) and the trade-off (what it costs you).
-- Both are the APPROVED comment, split where it turns ("..., but ..."), word for word; six sentences
-- that do not turn that way were split by hand. `comment` itself is untouched, so the Room Concierge
-- shows exactly what it showed before.
-- A row is filled only where its comment is still the sentence that was split (md5 guard): a comment
-- reworded since gets nothing and the card falls back to the whole sentence.
ALTER TABLE public.conga_line_ratings ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS why_this_ship text;
ALTER TABLE public.conga_line_ratings ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS watch_for text;

UPDATE public.conga_line_ratings r
   SET why_this_ship = v.why, watch_for = v.watch
  FROM (VALUES
  ('adventure-of-the-seas','65e997fb9dc0e38140e3d65149b74b86','Adventure keeps itself up well for its age, and the crew cares.','Just know the food won''t surprise you and popular spots fill fast.'),
  ('allure-of-the-seas','4c2ea60199b52bd43a6ad362cb8b5e70','Allure''s a big ship with real standout spaces and staff that cares.','The main dining menu feels dated and pools get shoulder-to-shoulder.'),
  ('anthem-of-the-seas','c8cbdf30a8d5f9c3fcf65d81090a115e','Anthem''s cabins are spacious and comfortable.','The ship feels crowded in the spaces that matter most—buffet lines and pool decks get packed, which can wear on you over a week.'),
  ('arvia','f78404d3e2f0c7c1680252d26515695a','Arvia''s got modern spaces and good food options.','The crowds during school holidays can make basic services feel like a hassle.'),
  ('brilliance-of-the-seas','97f9691af3efdb2c3f634cd09869cfdc','Brilliance feels smaller and more human than the megaships, with light and views that make a real difference.','The kitchen struggles when she''s full.'),
  ('caribbean-princess','5031073e34a7400adccb40c3f18f4ed8','The crew works hard and makes you feel welcome.','The ship itself is tired — aging cabins, spotty AC, and food that''s lost its edge.'),
  ('carnival-adventure','27d39e6df2edd510ab72c125373d8677','The crew is the ship''s strength.','The cabins feel worn and the dining lines can test your patience, especially on school holidays.'),
  ('carnival-breeze','deec412ef131969f9e7d093be8ecad4f','Breeze is a solid value with a crew that cares.','The buffet lines and food quality hold it back from being a real standout.'),
  ('carnival-celebration','8113841d5c1d9d807d2d2b309b06574c','Celebration feels like a real step up for Carnival.','The dining room gets stretched thin when the ship fills up, so manage your expectations there.'),
  ('carnival-conquest','1e149d556e1736ef9743b6f2941fb18f','The crew makes this ship work.','Conquest is older and it shows—thin walls mean noise from neighbors, and the pool deck gets tight when it''s full.'),
  ('carnival-dream','c5473e14fecec76e8a10c6a678001658','Dream''s crew knows your name and looks after you.','The ship runs loud and the cabin details feel a step behind.'),
  ('carnival-elation','428674a9266bf1f65e18e219a259cc16','Elation is a straightforward, no-frills ship with a crew that cares.','The ship itself feels cramped and tired, and there''s not much to do once the sun goes down.'),
  ('carnival-encounter','85af4fd7a8b633c481cdd89e8030990e','Encounter''s cabins are spacious and the beds are comfortable.','The ship itself is showing its age—things break, smells linger, and the food won''t impress you.'),
  ('carnival-firenze','3d1ad58f31d482f334284fd1f9371e8a','Firenze is clean and feels newer than most Carnivals.','The crowds on the pool deck and at the elevators can wear on you fast.'),
  ('carnival-freedom','37244332a80f82f9240e11cc7a705b4c','Freedom''s crew cares and it shows.','You''re sailing an older ship where the noise and crowds can wear on you if you prefer a quieter getaway.'),
  ('carnival-glory','80229e4f1720602e78adf6f18af15e8e','Glory''s crew is why people rebook her.','The ship itself is showing its age—plumbing hiccups and worn spaces that newer ships have already fixed.'),
  ('carnival-horizon','46aae588623d69e04f9b1da9e03c38e6','Horizon''s cabins and crew really shine.','Expect long embarkation lines and crowded public spaces on a nearly four-thousand-person ship.'),
  ('carnival-jubilee','14c35c5da7bfd34565b8bcd49804680d','Jubilee feels less crowded than a Carnival ship her size has any right to.','The Galveston embarkation will test your patience.'),
  ('carnival-legend','8c71011007a8391e2e73ebfebd8f43b1','Legend''s a smaller, slower ship with real charm and a relaxed crowd.','The galley hasn''t kept up with the rest of the vessel.'),
  ('carnival-liberty','ec2dd943643247140a2f2f42986a8e94','Liberty''s crew makes you feel welcome from the moment you board.','The ship''s age shows in the cabins and common areas, which matters if you''re sensitive to wear.'),
  ('carnival-luminosa','9ae08a2ba0d649e07982e53925a9156a','Luminosa shines on Alaska and Mexico routes where the scenery does the heavy lifting.','The ship itself feels older and nickels-and-dimes you in ways newer Carnival vessels don''t.'),
  ('carnival-magic','e412b12bbaecf8b4ce18e33aca383413','Magic is solid on the basics—your cabin will be comfortable and the crew will take care of you.','She''s been a little rough around the edges lately, and crowds can wear thin on popular sailings.'),
  ('carnival-miracle','ca6dafa7a20f48097f976bdbcf800c0f','Miracle''s the right pick if crowding bothers you — it''s small enough that you''ll grab a lounger without fighting for it.','You''re trading the newer-ship extras for that breathing room.'),
  ('carnival-panorama','e1452382cac91aed462837f810d753f0','Panorama''s a newer ship with real polish and solid service.','The food hasn''t kept pace with the rest of the vessel.'),
  ('carnival-paradise','0e232ce72f4eb5900cce5818eac5de61','Paradise is a small, easy escape from Tampa where the crew cares.','The ship itself is showing its age and the entertainment lineup feels thin.'),
  ('carnival-pride','f558ab53be12305d62568d4970212493','Pride''s got a loyal crew and the Baltimore homeport is hard to beat.','The cabins run cold and dinner doesn''t match what you get at breakfast.'),
  ('carnival-radiance','fc67a2756100ee00f0d5806c69269cb8','Radiance has a crew that cares and shows it every day.','The cabins are tight and the main dining room lags behind the specialty spots.'),
  ('carnival-spirit','926ba817d7dc8ca6c6ae72436ef0fbc7','Spirit shines on the Alaska run where the scenery does most of the work.','The buffet and slow service responses can wear thin on longer sailings.'),
  ('carnival-splendor','7cd7b24f26d3ac73ad61acfe570e7874','Splendor''s a family ship with real comfortable cabins and good beds.','It''s loud and busy — book a suite if you want any peace.'),
  ('carnival-sunrise','27a7457eddb5cc53ee79cc9409458ed2','Sunrise is a solid value for a short family getaway from Miami.','The crew and housekeeping won''t make up for crowded pools and smoke that drifts into the hallways.'),
  ('carnival-sunshine','71083547be884910736f0e1eb3a2b426','Sunshine wins on staff and convenience from the home ports.','The layout takes real getting used to and the pool won''t fit everyone at once.'),
  ('carnival-valor','0c994f894bceae6cfcfa9861b4d44e89','Valor''s crew and New Orleans homeport make the embark smooth and the onboard feel warm.','She''s an older ship with cabin layouts that can surprise you.'),
  ('carnival-venezia','fe3ad53de2fefbd5226d4f283783bb32','Venezia is a beautiful ship with real style and cabins with balconies that make the sailing feel special.','The galley can''t keep up with the lines at lunch.'),
  ('carnival-vista','a19e2c4db64611bad8fad8d9bee7c854','Vista''s built for families and it shows—great energy and activities for kids.','The crowds and tight schedules mean you''ll spend a lot of time waiting in line.'),
  ('celebrity-apex','ce1bcc3c62e70d6fcd2cac4957a5c3d6','Apex pampers you with sleek design and top-tier dining if you book AquaClass.','You''ll pay for it, and quiet spots to decompress are hard to find.'),
  ('celebrity-ascent','3d97e5d825eaf5ab705dd64f7833237c','Ascent is a beautifully modern ship that runs like clockwork.','You''re paying premium prices for a decidedly grown-up experience with little to do if you''ve got kids in tow.'),
  ('celebrity-beyond','65fc9576c3ad759ccbeec3da98a74704','Beyond has gorgeous spaces and the food is excellent.','You''re paying a premium price for a ship that feels less exclusive than it used to.'),
  ('celebrity-constellation','abaa6b6177a59b7291e46b988724600a','Constellation has real elegance and a loyal following.','Service can feel thin on some sailings, especially in the dining room.'),
  ('celebrity-eclipse','a4f88ba996acb75297af51e0d71ba5c1','Eclipse excels at food and service.','The ship itself is starting to show its age in ways that matter if you''re picky about your surroundings.'),
  ('celebrity-edge','2d195cd43fa40500e8f02704b4c38100','Edge is built for quiet and comfort—great cabins, solid food, crew that knows your name.','You''ll feel the slow pace if you''re after nonstop action.'),
  ('celebrity-equinox','01e24e9577b0deb1463a729c9e1a3d94','Equinox''s crew will make you feel welcome.','The ship itself shows its age—rust on balconies and worn cabin fabrics are real issues that housekeeping can''t quite keep ahead of.'),
  ('celebrity-flora','ab6f6a32de37c2338398f75a62d33420','Flora is built for real exploration—naturalist-led landings in the Galapagos are the whole trip.','You''re paying expedition prices and need to be ready to get out of your cabin and onto the islands every day.'),
  ('celebrity-infinity','87ef4fa15e51681c69b271106d7c4592','Infinity shines on Greek itineraries and with a crew that cares.','The ship itself feels tired — chipped paint, mildewed bathrooms, long dinner lines when it''s full.'),
  ('celebrity-millennium','b6e66abda201f60f3f50bb319e1aab7b','Millennium shines on Asia itineraries where the ports do the heavy lifting.','The ship itself feels its age and the dining doesn''t match what you''d expect from Celebrity.'),
  ('celebrity-reflection','40d7169c941c55850e85e11422625902','Reflection runs tight and clean with a crew that keeps up even when the ship is full, and the food lands across every venue.',NULL),
  ('celebrity-silhouette','c8208cb4ea3bbb5be104f7154f7712fd','Silhouette shines on the itineraries—Iceland, Greenland, Bermuda.','The food and shows don''t quite match what you''d get on newer premium ships.'),
  ('celebrity-solstice','149059580b326e69e041e385e1eb14e9','Solstice feels fresh after her refit and the theater shows move people.','The buffet is a real letdown — you''ll eat better in the specialty restaurants.'),
  ('celebrity-summit','39a42df6fedc513f94074f040f0509cd','Summit shines on Alaska and Panama routes where the views do the work.','The ship itself is showing its age — rusty railings and worn furniture remind you she''s been around the block.'),
  ('celebrity-xcel','4bc5a961bb3e1679e07187c040bedaf7','Xcel is a new ship with excellent food and a crew that seems to care.','The Infinite Verandas take getting used to if you want a real open balcony.'),
  ('coral-princess','8e0278773ac924cd0f4819c9cfb64cd8','Coral Princess shines on Alaska and Panama Canal routes where the itinerary does the heavy lifting.','The ship itself feels quiet and a touch tired.'),
  ('costa-smeralda','3578fed444782018bd462e383b44f84d','Smeralda''s a beautiful ship and the Mediterranean itinerary shines.','The nickel-and-diming on basics like water and coffee wears thin fast.'),
  ('costa-toscana','ca0eef9ea12c1574c6430c21fbddb704','Toscana is a beautiful ship in the right ports.','The food and service won''t pamper you unless you pay extra on top of your already-cheap fare.'),
  ('crown-princess','180d43eaaf16ba742ea985a49db014ff','Crown Princess handles the long exotic routes beautifully.','The ship itself shows its age — worn spaces and smaller cabins are the trade-off for those far-flung itineraries.'),
  ('diamond-princess','0d6952972b297042e7bc3fe67891f0e7','Diamond Princess shines on Japan itineraries—the destination and cherry-blossom timing are the real draw.','The ship itself feels its age, especially in cramped bathrooms where showers and plumbing can be temperamental.'),
  ('discovery-princess','81142b0834b9b858914c92e10af70d02','Discovery Princess is beautifully kept and comfortable in your cabin.','Dining quality swings wildly depending on where and when you eat.'),
  ('emerald-princess','13769106a47b7afbc1117a20247b7fd1','Emerald Princess keeps herself up well for her years.','The galley''s split personality means your dinner experience hinges on where you eat—the specialty spots shine while the main room leaves you wanting.'),
  ('enchanted-princess','b518115732385d78698f1492d5291b4b','Enchanted Princess is impressive to look at and her shows are first-rate.','Expect worn bedding and the occasional lukewarm plate in the main dining room.'),
  ('enchantment-of-the-seas','9b3170ee1ee236c6fa771e0ea80bd253','Enchantment trades fancy for honest value and a crew that remembers your name.','Don''t expect a polished newer ship.'),
  ('explorer-of-the-seas','c3947eb0fdd4416b3ad6e5ed9e4f71dd','Explorer''s crew is solid.','The ship''s aging — worn carpets, tired furniture — shows the cost-cutting clearly.'),
  ('freedom-of-the-seas','9e4284f36ce0522df7b34e1d37b1da44','Freedom''s crew really does make the difference—warm and attentive.','The main dining room food won''t wow you, so plan to eat elsewhere.'),
  ('grand-princess','28cf73832db96a2c6eba722e43d050f0','Grand Princess wins you over with a crew that enjoys the work.','You''ll pay for that warmth in administrative headaches and confusing bills.'),
  ('grandeur-of-the-seas','9f8c5b8574cf92d1204f49bb05cf6d44','Grandeur''s real strength is a crew that feels invested in your trip.','The ship itself shows her age in the cabins and galley.'),
  ('harmony-of-the-seas','f5033fb1965acd2d3f8ff7e403d3bd79','Harmony keeps you entertained and the crew really cares.','On rough seas you''ll fight for a deck chair and the food leans toward repetitive.'),
  ('icon-of-the-seas','cd823130a3183e1f5ab3c1e668512ed5','Icon is a real family ship with excellent food and staff.','You''ll pay extra for most of the fun once you''re on board.'),
  ('independence-of-the-seas','adb73d114bb3fe158da044e60f48926e','Independence has a crew that cares.','The ship feels crowded on sea days and the dining outside the main restaurant can disappoint.'),
  ('iona','fc1372e46c2af614e16cbee9aa491c07','Iona''s a beautiful ship with real spaces to breathe.','The crew''s stretched thin—you''ll wait a long time for a drink in the evenings.'),
  ('island-princess','1d5892ed049604e0628c8fed6adfc360','Island Princess has itineraries you won''t find on bigger ships, and a crew that goes the extra mile.','You trade modern cabins and flash for them.'),
  ('jewel-of-the-seas','9fee777486b8572a0137094e4542758b','Jewel feels like a real ship rather than a floating mall, and the crew makes you feel looked after.','The dining can leave you wanting if you''re picky about food.'),
  ('liberty-of-the-seas','0a55fe543e3462f1c4e0779c3c1c1047','Liberty''s crew cares and keeps things running.','The dining room lags behind what you''d expect even after the recent overhaul, so eat elsewhere when you can.'),
  ('majestic-princess','f46e17da0140f5d2319b7861e5c83e11','Majestic Princess is built for real itineraries—the British Isles and Baltic routes are special.','Cabin comfort is uneven, and you''ll notice the nickel-and-diming.'),
  ('mardi-gras','3e925096ff0d46fe9e5a1bfe96dd60af','Mardi Gras feeds you better than you''d expect for the price.','The ship''s already showing scuffs that make you wonder how well she''ll age.'),
  ('margaritaville-at-sea-islander','7f91d3c44e1e6ea06f682748fe987b52','The Islander surprises you with how well it''s built and maintained for the price, and the crew cares.','The party vibe means you won''t find a quiet corner.'),
  ('margaritaville-at-sea-paradise','1e6fbe0f5aad77a44ee1e0a5d6099f7d','Margaritaville trades newness for a crew that knows your name and rooms that feel bigger than they should.','Just don''t expect the ship itself to surprise you.'),
  ('mariner-of-the-seas','8b877b192bdb7b0cf8bd556d5a2bb2a1','Mariner packs real activity and moves fast.','Cabins show their age—stains and tired bathrooms are a real complaint.'),
  ('msc-armonia','80ed250d0ea759ed3989d5956ab302c0','Armonia''s crew will treat you like family.','The buffet won''t impress you and the ship itself feels tired—worth it mainly if the price and ports are right.'),
